  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The linear system of equations\r\n$\\left.\\begin{array}{l}8 x-3 y-5 z=0 \\\\ 5 x-8 y+3 z=0 \\\\ 3 x+5 y-8 z=0\\end{array}\\right\\}$ has",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Drw74",
      "text": "only zero solution",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4bHq9",
      "text": "only finite number of non-zero solutions",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "1Qf67",
      "text": "no non-zero solution",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kUmk7",
      "text": "infinitely many non-zero solutions",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, \r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\n& 8x-3 y-5 z=0 \\\\\r\n& 5 x-8 y+3 z=0 \\\\\r\n& 3 x+5 y-8 z=0 \\\\\r\n&D=\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}\r\n8 & -3 & -5 \\\\\r\n5 & -8 & 3 \\\\\r\n3 & 5 & -8\r\n\\end{array}\\right| \\\\\r\n&=8(64-15)+3(-40-9)-5(25+24) \\\\\r\n=& 8 \\times 49+3 \\times(-49)-5 \\times 49 \\\\\r\n=& 0\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$\r\n$\\therefore$ The system has infinitely many non-zero solutions.",
    "image": null
  },
